/*
 * guatiao-serde -- reading and writing a guatiao value as a document.
 *
 * GENERATED BY cbindgen, from build.rs. DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
 * Regenerate with:
 *   GUATIAO_WRITE_HEADER=1 cargo build -p guatiao-serde --features c-header,json,toml,yaml
 *
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 * EMITTING ANSWERS A VALUE, NOT A STRING.
 *
 * guatiao_json_emit() and friends write a guatiao_value holding the text,
 * which you release with guatiao_value_free() like any other tree. There
 * is no second thing to free, and the answer carries the allocator that
 * made it.
 *
 * The `how` argument is one integer: its LOW BYTE chooses how a byte
 * string is spelled where the format has none, and the bits above it are
 * flags. Zero is the default in every position.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 * EVERY `out` IS WRITTEN ABSENT ON ENTRY.
 *
 * Before anything can fail, so a caller reading it after an error reads
 * GUATIAO_ABSENT, the same convention guatiao.h and guatiao_intake.h
 * follow. `out` must not hold a tree you still own.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 * WHERE A PARSE STOPPED.
 *
 * guatiao_json_parse_ex() and its TOML and YAML twins take one more
 * pointer, a guatiao_parse_error that may be NULL. A document that does
 * not parse fills it with the format, the line and the column (from 1,
 * 0 when unknown) and a `message` string value, released with
 * guatiao_value_free(). The message never quotes the document, which may
 * hold a secret.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 * A FORMAT IS A BUILD-TIME CHOICE, SO ITS DECLARATIONS ARE GUARDED.
 *
 * Only JSON is on by default. The TOML and YAML functions are in the
 * library only when it was built with those features, so this header
 * declares them only when you say the same thing:
 *
 *   cc -DGUATIAO_SERDE_TOML -DGUATIAO_SERDE_YAML ...
 *
 * Define the macro for each feature the library you link was built with.
 * Without it the declaration is absent, which is an error at the call
 * rather than a link failure nobody sees until later.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

